====================================================================
MODULE 1: DISCOVERY
====================================================================

A) Connection and Interface Discovery
-------------------------------------

1) Command:
show hostname
Used for:
- Verifying firewall identity.
- Confirming connection to the correct ASA device.

2) Command:
show route
Used for:
- Checking default route (0.0.0.0/0).
- Identifying the internet-facing (outside) interface.

3) Command:
show run interface | include nameif
Used for:
- Validating logical interface roles (outside/inside/dmz).
- Confirming that the expected outside interface role exists.

4) Command:
show interface <interface_name>
Example:
show interface outside
Used for:
- Verifying interface operational state (up/down).
- Extracting interface IP address.
- Confirming correct outside interface selection.

B) VPN Tunnel Discovery
-----------------------

5) Command:
show crypto ikev1 sa
Used for:
- Checking Phase-1 (IKE) Security Associations.
- Validating IKE negotiation status for peers.

6) Command:
show crypto ipsec sa
Used for:
- Checking Phase-2 (IPsec) Security Associations.
- Validating encrypted traffic flow using packet counters.

7) Command:
show run crypto map
Used for:
- Reading VPN policy mapping.
- Extracting crypto map name.
- Extracting sequence number.
- Extracting peer IP address.
- Identifying ACL and transform-set association.

C) Tunnel Status Logic
----------------------

Logic:
- If peer IP is present in show crypto ikev1 sa OR show crypto ipsec sa:
  Tunnel status = UP
- If peer IP is absent in both:
  Tunnel status = DOWN

Used for:
- Generating tunnel inventory with live status.

====================================================================
MODULE 2: RESET
====================================================================

A) Pre-Reset Validation
-----------------------

1) Command:
show crypto ikev1 sa
Used for:
- Checking current Phase-1 state before reset.

2) Command:
show crypto ipsec sa
Used for:
- Checking current Phase-2 session/traffic state before reset.

3) Command:
show run crypto map
Used for:
- Identifying correct peer IP and crypto map tunnel reference.

B) Reset Execution
------------------

4) Command:
vpn-sessiondb logoff tunnel-group <peer-ip>
Example:
vpn-sessiondb logoff tunnel-group 4.227.229.249
Used for:
- Terminating active/stale VPN session for selected peer.
- Forcing tunnel renegotiation.

C) Post-Reset Validation
------------------------

5) Command:
show crypto ikev1 sa
Used for:
- Verifying fresh/rebuilt Phase-1 session after reset.

6) Command:
show crypto ipsec sa
Used for:
- Verifying fresh/rebuilt Phase-2 session after reset.

====================================================================
MODULE 3: UPDATE
====================================================================

A) Session Preparation
----------------------

1) Command:
terminal pager 0
Used for:
- Disabling CLI pagination (--More--).
- Ensuring uninterrupted full output for automation parsing.

B) Target VPN Validation
------------------------

2) Command:
show run tunnel-group <peer-ip>
Example:
show run tunnel-group 4.227.229.249
Used for:
- Verifying selected tunnel-group exists before applying updates.

3) Command:
show run crypto map
Used for:
- Identifying crypto map name and sequence.
- Identifying peer mapping.
- Identifying ACL binding.
- Identifying active transform-set.

4) Command:
show run access-list <acl_name>
Example:
show run access-list outside_cryptomap_1
Used for:
- Reading current encryption domain entries.
- Identifying local-to-remote subnet rules currently active.

C) Object and Object-Group Resolution
-------------------------------------

5) Command:
show run object-group id <group_name>
Example:
show run object-group id AZURE_PA_NET
Used for:
- Listing object members inside VPN ACL object-group.

6) Command:
show run
Used for:
- Parsing object network definitions.
- Resolving object names into actual subnet/mask values.

D) Display Current VPN Configuration Before Change
--------------------------------------------------

Commands:
show run tunnel-group <peer-ip>
show run crypto map
show run access-list <acl_name>

Used for:
- Presenting current peer, subnet policy, and transform-set details.
- Preventing accidental updates on wrong tunnel/policy.

E) Update Operations (Detailed)
-------------------------------

Operation 1: Update Peer IP
---------------------------
Command:
crypto map <map_name> <seq> set peer <new-peer-ip>
Used for:
- Updating remote VPN endpoint IP.

Optional (if new peer tunnel-group is needed):
tunnel-group <new-peer-ip> type ipsec-l2l
tunnel-group <new-peer-ip> ipsec-attributes
 ikev1 pre-shared-key <psk>
Used for:
- Creating peer tunnel-group.
- Assigning authentication key for new peer.

Operation 2: Update Local Subnet
---------------------------------
Add command:
access-list <acl_name> extended permit ip <new_local_subnet> <new_local_mask> <remote_subnet> <remote_mask>
Used for:
- Adding new local encryption domain.

Replace commands:
no access-list <acl_name> extended permit ip <old_local_subnet> <old_local_mask> <remote_subnet> <remote_mask>
access-list <acl_name> extended permit ip <new_local_subnet> <new_local_mask> <remote_subnet> <remote_mask>
Used for:
- Replacing old local subnet with new local subnet safely.

Operation 3: Update Remote Subnet
----------------------------------
Add command:
access-list <acl_name> extended permit ip <local_subnet> <local_mask> <new_remote_subnet> <new_remote_mask>
Used for:
- Adding new remote encryption domain.

Replace commands:
no access-list <acl_name> extended permit ip <local_subnet> <local_mask> <old_remote_subnet> <old_remote_mask>
access-list <acl_name> extended permit ip <local_subnet> <local_mask> <new_remote_subnet> <new_remote_mask>
Used for:
- Replacing old remote subnet with new remote subnet.

Operation 4: Update Phase-2 Encryption
--------------------------------------
Command:
crypto map <map_name> <seq> set ikev1 transform-set <new_transform_set>
Used for:
- Updating IPsec Phase-2 transform-set policy.

Operation 5: Update PSK
-----------------------
Command:
tunnel-group <peer-ip> ipsec-attributes
 ikev1 pre-shared-key <new_psk>
Used for:
- Rotating/updating pre-shared key for selected peer.

F) Post-Update Verification and Save
------------------------------------

21) Command:
show crypto ikev1 sa
Used for:
- Verifying Phase-1 status after updates.

22) Command:
show crypto ipsec sa
Used for:
- Verifying Phase-2 status and traffic after updates.

23) Command:
write memory
Used for:
- Saving running configuration to startup configuration.

